 $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =4y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(2Ax-3b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(2\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-48 \\\\ -32\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-240 & 0 & -96 \\\\ -160 & 0 & -64\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186670010 "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}=-5.\n$$"] [17592186670048 "We proceed to find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\left(-\\frac{3}{3}\\right)\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}=2.\n$$"] [17592186670073 "We find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bm